{"kind":"event","event_id":5009,"event_uid":"01M2KQV0C6FC54YV7T2KDFJX84","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":226,"issue_uid":"01M2KP4Y0ZKARPDX4AZ0N175D8","issue_short_id":"75d8","actor":"impl:1@run-14","hlc_physical_ms":1789516415366,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"8555a2dada338489e9fc4cd295234a0370a45b1b468f28a9082051e11ce5413b","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2KQV0C5EFKZXC6BPDV7FAZP","author":"impl:1@run-14","body":"task 1 (trash table) starting at f24d405. Approach as the Context dictates: one shared todo-cells literal reused for `todos` and `trash` in TABLES_SCHEMA; `deleteTodo` becomes a single transaction (hasRow guard, delTable('trash'), setRow('trash', id, getRow('todos', id)), delRow('todos', id)); new `undoDelete(store)` a single transaction looping getRowIds('trash'); a second INVARIANTS entry for 'trash' that is the todos rule applied to a trashed row. Then the three new expected JSON files, and the loosening of the BASE pins (smoke, done-count leg (o), todos-store leg (c), and the four linter test files off exact counts/lists onto lower bounds and toContain). Not writing tests/state-exams/delete-to-trash.test.ts — a peer's exam lands there.","created_at":"2026-09-15T23:53:35.365134093Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T23:53:35.366Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5010,"event_uid":"01M2KR11C5MRVQ29TMKMYX7A9N","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":226,"issue_uid":"01M2KP4Y0ZKARPDX4AZ0N175D8","issue_short_id":"75d8","actor":"exam:1@run-14","hlc_physical_ms":1789516612997,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"5365fdd32231f642a55678ababf7f4c96193d6bc3c59080098c7a3050ba51778","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2KR11C34Y74VS3Z5F8RW25H","author":"exam:1@run-14","body":"examiner, exam for `tests/state-exams/delete-to-trash.test.ts`. Approach: one `stateExam` for leg (a) (the click on `.todoItem button` over the two-open seed, expected `two-open-todos-first-trashed.json`, the two views, the `{table:'trash',row:'0',absent:true}` mutant), then legs (b)-(k) as ordinary `bun:test` blocks beside it, the way `clear-completed.test.ts` is built.\n\nReading of the legs I am fixing now, so a later session does not have to reconstruct it:\n\n1. Every state assertion compares a store snapshot against the *parsed expected/seed file*, never against a content literal spelled inside the exam. The Global Check forbids pinning the key set of a todos row, and a content literal like `{text:'buy milk',completed:false}` is exactly that key set — the sibling run adding a cell to the todos literal would turn a green exam red at the fold. File-vs-store equality is the same assertion stated relatively, and it is also how the legs are worded ('snapshots deep-equal to the parsed …json').\n2. Where M1/M2 say what the file itself must hold ('which is exactly the M2 literal'), the exam pins the parts that are not a row's cell set: which tables are present in `content[0]`, which row ids each holds, and the named cells by value (`text`, `completed`) read cell by cell. So 'exactly the M2 literal' is asserted up to the cells the Global Check reserves for the sibling.\n3. M1's 'trash holds '0' with every cell the todos row held' is asserted relatively: the trash row `toEqual` the *seed's* todos row '0'. A hand-picked subset of cells fails it whatever the schema grows to.\n4. Leg (k) runs each of the eight `Run:` lines verbatim through `bash -c` from the repository root (the `runLine` idiom `done-count.test.ts` already uses) and asserts exit 0, plus the two 'in place of the exact list' absences: no `toEqual([\\\"todos\\\"])` left in `smoke.test.ts`, no `toEqual(['todos'])` left in `done-count.test.ts`. It does not grep the four linter test files for a particular loosening — M9 leaves the shape to the implementer and only pins that the suite exits 0 and that `reachability.test.ts` carries zero `deleteTodo or setTodoCompleted` lines.\n5. The three expected `.json` files are the implementer's to create, so the exam creates no fixture: at BASE their absence is part of the absent implementation, and the `readFileSync` failure names the missing path.","created_at":"2026-09-15T23:56:52.995646844Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T23:56:52.997Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5013,"event_uid":"01M2KR7G7T23S7TEGV0XWCXR37","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":226,"issue_uid":"01M2KP4Y0ZKARPDX4AZ0N175D8","issue_short_id":"75d8","actor":"exam:1@run-14","hlc_physical_ms":1789516824826,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"ff2ac6ba6680dc5a7cb02f39b6fbd3ee490b1cdef046a768a3086027a4f944c5","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2KR7G7R2R3Y86J4XHXSHQ8Y","author":"exam:1@run-14","body":"exam handed in: `tests/state-exams/delete-to-trash.test.ts`, 21 registered tests (one `stateExam` + 20 blocks), every leg (a)-(k) encoded, nothing under `unsatisfiable`.\n\nMeasured here, in this tree:\n\n- At BASE, red for exactly one reason — `SyntaxError: Export named 'undoDelete' not found in module client/src/storeData.ts`. Nothing else in the file is reachable until that export exists, which is the absent implementation and not a typo or a missing fixture.\n- Against a throwaway prototype of the Context's own implementation (the shared `TODO_CELLS` literal under `todos` and `trash`, `deleteTodo` as hasRow/delTable/setRow/delRow in one transaction, `undoDelete` as the getRowIds loop, the second INVARIANTS entry, and the three expected `.json` files) plus the three pinned-file loosenings of M9: **19 pass, 2 fail**. The two fails are `bun test packages/tinyapp-lint` and the `deleteTodo or setTodoCompleted` grep — i.e. exactly the four linter-test loosenings the prototype did not do. Legs (a)-(j) and six of the eight `Run:` lines were green.\n- Leg (a) really opens the page: the evidence run recorded `browser: ran`, `render: ran`, `action_ms` ~123 ms, and `mutant: {killed: true, path: 'trash/0'}` — the click on `.todoItem button` reaches the expected state and the mutant that drops the trash row is killed. The prototype was reverted; the tree is BASE plus the exam file only.\n\nTwo notes for whoever implements this:\n\n- Leg (j) asserts `files.length >= 10` over `state-exams/seeds` + `state-exams/expected` — a lower bound (3 seeds + 4 BASE expected + this task's 3), never an equality, so a sibling adding a snapshot does not turn it red.\n- The last leg-(k) block asserts the *absence* of `toEqual([\\\"todos\\\"])` in `smoke.test.ts` and of `toEqual(['todos'])` in `done-count.test.ts`, on top of the Proof's greps: a file keeping the old exact list beside a new `toContain` would pass every `Run:` line and still go red at the fold. It also asserts `done-count` carries `toContain('completed')` and `toContain('text')`, which is M9's leg (o) in words. Nothing greps the four linter test files for a particular shape — M9 leaves that to the implementer and only pins that the suite exits 0.","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:24.824844671Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:24.826Z"}
